        "original_id": "6fd2d26f-d2b6-5567-834c-ef70299b095f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Iva Pacetti, Arrigo Boito\n- Works: Mefistofele\n- Places: Loew's Lexington Theatre, New York City, La Scala, Milan\n- Topics: opera premieres, performances\n\nFacts:\n- Mefistofele is the only completed opera composed by the Italian composer-librettist Arrigo Boito.\n- Mefistofele is structured as a prologue, four acts, and an epilogue.\n- Mefistofele premiered on 5 March 1868 at La Scala in Milan under the baton of Arrigo Boito, despite his lack of experience and skill as a conductor.\n- Iva Pacetti reprised the role the year after the previously mentioned performance at Loew's Lexington Theatre in New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d76494ab-8848-5954-b9ef-2bbbd96e6c00",
        "text": "Page: Iva Pacetti. Sentence: She reprised the role the following year at Loew's Lexington Theatre in New York City.\nPage: Mefistofele. Sentence: Mefistofele (] ) is an opera in a prologue, four acts and an epilogue, the only completed opera with music by the Italian composer-librettist Arrigo Boito (there are several completed operas for which he was librettist only).\nPage: Mefistofele. Sentence: The opera was given its premiere on 5 March 1868 at La Scala, Milan, under the baton of the composer, despite his lack of experience and skill as a conductor.",
